WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.952
Base, instruct, and chat checkpoints can belong to the same model family but behave differently because of post-training

00:00:07.952 --> 00:00:14.887
and expected input format. Consider the same intent: summarize a paragraph in one sentence.

00:00:14.887 --> 00:00:18.207
A base model may simply continue the text.

00:00:18.207 --> 00:00:22.672
An instruct checkpoint is more likely to treat the sentence as a task.

00:00:22.672 --> 00:00:30.497
A chat checkpoint expects role-based messages and can use system, user, and assistant turns.

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:34.904
The model family matters, but the checkpoint type matters too.
